      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's a bit too vague and soft. the legal team is going to say this doesn't actually disclose enough. we need to get that compliance score up so it doesn't get flagged as \"under-disclosed,\" but like i said, it has to be professional. \n\ncan you try again? make the warnings more explicit and substantial so we actually hit a higher score on the scanner, but keep it sounding like a real financial document. don't just repeat the same word, but make sure those specific terms—risk, warning, caution—are integrated into actual, meaningful sentences about the fund's volatility.",
